Revised Privacy statement
Data We Collect
	Callego only collects data that is necessary to be able to provide the best business services for our customers.  This may include things such as contact information, account information, payment information, and transaction information. We only collect information that we need for the specific purpose it is being used for. We may also collect information that is non-personal in nature and can’t be used to identify you. Callego will also try to keep information as up to date as possible.
How we collect data
	We collect data directly from customers when they use or purchase our services. We also collect information when you create an account or otherwise communicate with us. We also receive information from third parties such as business partners or service providers. We process any information received in accordance with the law.
How we use Data
	Callego uses personal data only for specific business purposes. These purposes may include the following:
•	Process and manage customer accounts
•	Maintain and improve products and services
•	Communicating with customers
•	Provide customer support
•	Develop new products and services
•	Comply with legal and regulatory requirements
•	Detect and investigate fraud
We will not use the personal data for any purpose other than what it was collected for. We will comply with all GDPR guidelines.
Data Sharing and Third Parties
	Callego may share personal data with trusted third parties such as service providers, suppliers and affiliates that need the information to help provide business services. Any third party will be required to follow all GDPR guidelines to work with us. We do not sell any data that is prohibited by the law.
How we store Data
	We will store data on Callego’s networks, at corporate offices, and on systems authorized by third parties.  We maintain standard safeguards to protect personal data against unauthorized access, destruction, and damage. These safeguards include role-based access controls, encryption, and security training for employees. All personnel information is limited to organizations and individuals who have a legitimate business need to access it.
